&reftitle.description;
stringfalsesession_name stringnullname&null;
session_name returns the name of the current session. If name is given, session_name will update the session name and return the old session name.
If a new session name is supplied, session_name modifies the HTTP cookie (and outputs the content when session.use_trans_sid is enabled). If a session is active or the headers have already been sent (any output that is not buffered), calling session_name with a name raises an E_WARNING and returns &false;. session_name must be called before session_start for the session to work properly.
The session name is reset to the default value stored in session.name at request startup time. Thus, you need to call session_name for every request (and before session_start is called).

&reftitle.errors;

 Throws a ValueError if
 name contains a NUL byte.

  &reftitle.examples;



    session_name example


<?php

/* set the session name to WebsiteID */

$previous_name = session_name("WebsiteID");

echo "The previous session name was $previous_name<br />";
?>
